# Documentation policy

## Hierarchy

`docs/EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md` wins over all subordinate "next steps". Reports are dated point-in-time evidence; mark SUPERSEDED when replaced and point back to the backlog.

## Naming and placement

- Lowercase hyphenated markdown names for new docs.
- ADRs in `docs/adr/` (accepted only with repo evidence; else `PROPOSED-*.md`).
- Architecture in `docs/diagrams/` + `docs/reference/`.
- Experiment cards in `research/offseason_2026/experiments/`.
- Historical reports in `docs/reference/reports/`.
- Skill docs in `docs/agent/`.

## Rules

- `CONTEXT.md` holds glossary + lifecycle + grains + paths. Do not paste reports into it.
- Cite n, Brier/skill, ECE, ROI/WR, CLV to a file or report key. Cite golden metrics; do not recompute.
- Prefer links to canonical docs over duplicating procedures.
- Research scripts stay ASCII-only (cp1252 consoles).
